# Shell scripts must keep LF endings even when checked out on Windows.
#
# The Docker image is built from the working tree, not from git, so a CRLF
# checkout of entrypoint.sh ships a "#!/bin/sh\r" shebang into the image. The
# kernel then looks for an interpreter literally named "/bin/sh\r" and the
# container dies with "/entrypoint.sh: not found" -- which reads as a missing
# file rather than a line-ending problem, and restarts forever.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for anything else executed inside a container.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
docker/entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
